From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: preserve PAN events and propagate mux errors

Queue bounded generation-tagged notifications instead of overwriting shared worker state. Keep consumption ACKs independent of mux success, correct the DP pin VDO bitmask, reject invalid fields, and quarantine ambiguous ACK/overflow sessions. Preserve disconnect cleanup on service loss. This does not establish applied QMP state, IRQ delivery to a Uke DP controller or physical display readiness.


Route asynchronous type-2 notifications separately from type-1 acknowledgements.

Acknowledge consumed events before potentially blocking mux/AUX work; recheck the session after the ACK.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -95,6 +95,15 @@
 
